  "query_preview": "/Sunday through Thursday/...\nIssued 248 AM MST THU NOV 5 2026\nThe pattern through the extended will consist of a broad upper \nlevel ridge extending across the western/central CONUS while a \nlongwave trough persists over the Gulf of Alaska and clips the\nPacific Northwest. This will place our area in southwest flow\naloft and keep temperatures 10-15 degrees above normal. A \nsystem moving across Washington on Sunday and another weak \nsystem on Monday will produce a 10-20% chance of showers across \nthe north with only increased clouds to the south. Additional \nsystems will move to the north through midweek, with \nprecipitation chances gradually rising to 20-30% across the \nnorth by Thursday. Winds will be breezy on Sunday and again\nWednesday/Thursday as systems pass by to the north. However, \nlight winds Monday and Tuesday and the ridge of high pressure \nmay result in stagnant valley conditions and temperature \ninversions.",
